            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "00fe897f-b004-49c3-bf82-4b733d0ab298",
                "key": "e4111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "MCP makes complexity feel approachable"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "intro",
                    "value": "A protocol becomes powerful when it helps more people do more with less ceremony."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "f3111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
                        "mediaKey": "5b10a9f0-dc4d-4770-bdb7-5b73abbf69ca",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "f8376009-7dd5-433e-8eee-b7609051194f",
                "key": "e4222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP is awesome for a second reason: it lowers the cost of trying something new. A tool can publish a clear capability, and an assistant can discover it without a bespoke integration for every possible workflow.</p><p>That creates a healthy ecosystem. Editors get better experiences, developers keep ownership of their systems, and teams can compose small capabilities into workflows that feel tailored to the moment.</p><p>The result is not automation for its own sake. It is a more generous interface to the systems we already depend on.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
